R-PA13 R-C6 R-C9 R-IX6 R-YK7 (slice 250, mutation gap G4): `tln install --offline` with a registry, the project p2 of patch/pa4-base-missing: json 2.2.0 is in the header (and in the cache), the patch has the base of json 2.1.0 (DBH2...), which is not in the cache. The index is Offline: the kept copy of GET /v1/packages/acme/json/releases has 2.1.0 and 2.2.0, and 2.1.0 is yanked.
R-PA13 finds the release that HAS the base hash. It is no pick: a yank must not hide the base (R-C6 says "not chosen for a new resolution"). So the release is found, and its fetch stops with --offline: exit 15, the text of the fetch (as run 4 of pa4-base-missing).
Fixed: `PickIndex.lookup!` reads the rows with no yank filter, so the base is found and its fetch stops (exit 15). The `calls.log` is from the reviewed run: the base dir check, one read of the kept copy, then `random` and `list_dirs packages` of the offline stop of `Fetch.packages!` (R-FE7).
Note: the argument `[x.entry.url]` of PatchApply is the header URL. When the base package is in the cache, no lookup is made, so the header URL never holds the base: mutant q11 cannot be caught by any case (see RESULT.md).
